# logs
*.log

# Firebase Android config — kept out of the public repo (origin is PUBLIC).
# Must exist locally for `expo run:android`.
#
# EAS Build gets it from the GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON file environment variable, which
# app.config.js copies to this directory before prebuild. Nothing needs committing:
#
#   eas env:set --name GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON --type file \
#     --value ./google-services.json --visibility secret \
#     --environment preview --environment production
#
# Do NOT go back to committing it in a temp commit to force it past EAS's VCS
# client. That dance also required deleting this line, and .gitignore is a
# fingerprint input — so every build came out with a runtime version no normal
# working tree could reproduce, and no OTA update would ever have matched it.
google-services.json
